  "summary": "I have been very interested in the advancement of technology in the health care industry for the past few years.  As a student at Tarleton State University in Stephenville, Texas, I wrote three research papers on the subject of electronic medical records.  This research gave me the desire to become involved in the transformation of paper and ink medical records to electronic medical records and bring medical records keeping into the twenty-first century.  \n\nI was a practicing nurse from 1974 until 1999. In January, 2003 I returned to college to obtain a degree in CIS with a programming and systems analysis emphasis.  I graduated with a BS in CIS in December, 2006. I believe that my experience as a nurse along with my most recent educational accomplishments would be very valuable to the electronic medical records industry and to your company.  I would appreciate the opportunity of being considered for the position of Entry Level Software Engineer in Temple that you have posted with LinkedIn.\n  \nI have attached my resume and will be happy to answer any questions that you might have regarding my work history or job qualifications.  I can be reached at my home number which is (254) 734-2176 or by cell phone (254) 631-2702 at any time and would be available for an interview at your convenience.  I look forward to hearing from you.  Thank you for your time and consideration.\n\nSpecialties: I was a practicing nurse for 25 years and understand the Medical Industry.  I am knowledgeable in medical terminology and practices.  I believe this experience would be valuable to any technology company that works with the medical industry to advance medical records or billing practices into the age of technology.",
